post.summary:
`POST /purchases/{purchase}/close` — partially received → closed short, with a reason;
nothing more can be received and nothing is owed for the missing units. 409 unless
partially received. Needs purchasing.create

`POST /orders/{order}/deliver` — shipped → delivered. A pending COD payment is marked
paid (the courier holds the cash: it is not cash in the ledger until remittance);
Finance recognises revenue from OrderDelivered. Needs orders.update + shipments.book

get.summary:
`GET /content/home/preview?locale=en|bn[&at=ISO]` — the DRAFT, for the builder's live
preview. Needs a valid, unexpired preview token from the admin in `X-Preview-Token`;
`at` previews the schedule at another instant. Never cache this response

`GET /payment-methods` — what checkout may offer now. COD is always first and default;
an online method appears only while its gateway is enabled (active, configured and —
in production — verified)

data.description:
Sorted rows, at most 1,000 (`truncated` says when there were more). Product rows
carry product_id/sku/category; category rows category_id/parent_id/products;
source rows `source` (`none` = not from a recommendation) and products.

ReviewSettlementLineRequest.description:
`POST /finance/settlements/{settlement}/items/{item}/review` — `decision` (accepted|excluded;
accept is for a `short` line only) and a `note` (required to exclude: why it is not booked).
Needs finance.reconcile_cod.

rider.description:
The delivery rider, recorded by staff when the rider calls (neither courier's API
returns it). `phone` is E.164 with customers.view_pii, else masked (`017****5678`);
`phone_masked` says which. Null when nobody has recorded one.

UpdateNotificationTemplateRequest.description:
`PUT /notifications/templates/{template}` — both bodies (EN + BN) in one document;
needs settings.update. A `{variable}` outside the template's allowlist is a 422 on that
field. Subject and preheader are required for email and ignored otherwise.
